# The bundled Node.js needs glibc 2.28 and the C++ runtime (checked against its symbol versions).
Depends: libc6 (>= 2.28), libgcc-s1 (>= 4.2), libstdc++6 (>= 6)
# Suggests, not Recommends: apt must never pull in a browser (on Ubuntu "chromium" is a snap).
# Without any of these Stick Note opens in the default browser, which works too.
Suggests: chromium | chromium-browser | google-chrome-stable | microsoft-edge-stable | brave-browser
Description: Personal whiteboard of sticky notes
 Stick Note is a private notes app with one endless whiteboard. Drag a paper
 slip onto the board, type a thought, paste a link or a screenshot, and leave
 it where it is: where you put a note is how you find it again.
 .
 Everything stays on your computer and works offline. The notes are saved in
 ~/.local/share/stick-note. The program runs in its own window when Chrome,
 Chromium, Edge or Brave is installed, and in your default browser otherwise.
 .
 A Node.js runtime is included, so nothing else needs to be installed.
